.TH LUKE "1" "October 2026" "Luke 0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
luke \- Use the source, Luke!
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B luke
[\fI\,OPTION\/\fR]... [\fI\,VAR=VALUE\/\fR]... [\fI\,TARGET\/\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Use the source, Luke!
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
print this help, then exit
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR
print version number, then exit
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
print the commands, without running them
.TP
\fB\-\-file\fR=\fI\,FILE\/\fR
use FILE instead of lukefile
.TP
\fB\-\-value\fR=\fI\,NAME\/\fR
print the value of variable NAME
.TP
\fB\-\-quiet\fR
without any output
.TP
\fB\-\-verbose\fR
provide more progress output
.PP
Each TARGET can be one of the module table keys from lukefile, or:
.TP
all
build all targets in lukefile
.TP
install
copy all built targets to $PREFIX
.TP
release
cut a release of the rock=NAME at version=VERSION
(rock=@package@ if not specified)
.PP
If no TARGET is given, 'all' is implied.
